parts.D:
CONCEPT: independent vectors each add a genuinely NEW direction;
   dependent vectors contain redundancy (at least one is a combination
   of the others).

parts.E:
CONDITIONS: holds for any matrix (any field). Also: rank(A) <=
   min(m, n); rank(A) = rank(A^T); rank(AB) <= min(rank A, rank B);
   rank(A^T A) = rank(A).

parts.D:
CONCEPT: A maps the line spanned by v onto itself. lambda > 1 stretches;
   0 < lambda < 1 shrinks; lambda < 0 flips direction; lambda = 0 means
   the vector is crushed to 0 (and A is singular).

parts.I:
MISTAKES: ordering eigenvectors and eigenvalues inconsistently;
   assuming every matrix is diagonalizable; using the formula for
   non-square matrices (use SVD instead).

parts.G:
EXAMPLES
   Simple: u = (1, 2, 2), v = (2, 0, 1): <u, v> = 2 + 0 + 2 = 4;
      |u| = 3, |v| = sqrt(5) = 2.236; 4 <= 3*2.236 = 6.708 OK;
      cos(theta) = 4/6.708 = 0.5963; theta approx 53.4 degrees.
   Moderate (functions): <f, g> = int[0..pi] sin x * 1 dx = 2 for f = sin,
      g = 1 on [0, pi]. |sin|^2 = int[0..pi] sin^2 = pi/2.

